    bao:BAO_0095009 obo:OBI_0001285 ;
    rdfs:comment "The samples in Pyrex and quartz test tubes were exposed to sunlight for 30 min with agitation in a water bath at 150 r.p.m. Similarly, corresponding samples were exposed under dark conditions, by wrapping the test samples in the test tubes with aluminium foils (solar irradiation outdoors: irradiance: UVA range = 3.979â€“4.652 mW/cm2; UVB range = 3.1â€“3.7 MED/h, where an MED is defined as the minimum erythemal dose or the amount of UV radiation to produce barely perceptible erythema; 1 MED/h = 0.05833 W/m2). The dark cytotoxicity and photo-induced cytotoxicity are examined as an united endpoint"@en ;
    skos:narrower mesh:D004926 .

