    rdfs:comment "Different toxicity threshold (% of Cellular viability) were tested: accuracies of 86.6% for viability decrease threshold larger than 20%(>EC20), 87.1%for viability decrease threshold of 25% (>EC25), and 87.3% for viability decrease threshold of 30% (>EC30). No statistical significance between them was considered. Dose-response curves were examined employing 3-(4,5-dimethylthiazol- 2-Yl)-2,5-diphenyltetrazolium bromide test (MTT), neutral red (NR), and Alamar blue as end point assays following 48- and 72-h exposures. Because cobalt NPs undergoes dissolution in aqueous media, we determined the dose-response curves for Co-ions, employing cobalt chloride for the same end points."@en ;
