    rdfs:comment "The agglomeration phenomenon largely influences toxicity of nanoparticles. Such properties of nanoparticles that describe their behavior are known as extrinsic properties. The ease of formation of agglomerates strongly depends on the surface charge that stabilizes dispersed nanoparticles and prevents them from agglomeration. However, the available experimental techniques are unable to measure surface charge directly; its value can only be estimated by measuring zeta potential (Î¶) in a given medium. Dynamic light scattering (DLS) was used zeta potential (Î¶) in cell culture media (serum-free) was done using a Malvern Instruments zeta-sizer Nano-ZS instrument."@en .

