    sio:SIO_000299 "The intravenous administration of GO or amine-derived GO (GO-NH2) into a mouse (250 μg/kg body weight) led to extensive pulmonary thromboembolism, which is consistent with the highly potent thrombogenic nature of GO, as previously shown in vitro; however, amine-GO (GO-NH2) was found to be less toxic compared with its unfunctionalized counterpart." ;
