  dc:description "In regulatory toxicology, the AGD is mandatory inclusions in OECD test guidelines used to test for developmental and reproductive toxicity of chemicals. Guidelines include &lsquo;TG 443 extended one-generation study&rsquo;, &lsquo;TG 421/422 reproductive toxicity screening studies&rsquo; and &lsquo;TG 414 developmental toxicity study&rsquo;."@en ;
  foaf:page <https://identifiers.org/aop/476> ;
  dcterms:license      <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

